  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that SureCN26387 may interact with SCCH-26 through multiple pathways, with the target entity SCCH-26 being a common endpoint in several relationships. Path 1 links SureCN26387 to Raji via a complex compound, which in turn targets SCCH-26. Path 2 connects SureCN26387 to Hepatocyte, which is targeted by Cocosamide B, ultimately leading to SCCH-26. Path 3 shows SureCN26387 targeting Raji, which is also targeted by Maplexin A, again leading to SCCH-26. These pathways collectively imply that SureCN26387 may act through different molecular mechanisms to influence SCCH-26, possibly through shared downstream targets or indirect interactions. The evidence supports a potential role for SureCN26387 in modulating SCCH-26, though the exact mechanism remains unclear due to the complexity of the target relationships.",
